      "before": "### 5.1 Principal class `repository-code` and its joins (R4)",
      "after": "### 5.1 Principal class `repository-code` and its joins (R4)\n\n**MWS-1 prospective Rust owner-source selection.** The exact CONTRACT.md and selection.json under docs/implementation/m3/snapshot-plan-c/native-workspace-owner-selection-r1/ select snapshot-member for an activated owner whose opaque package id is in workspace_members of the same admitted bundled metadata observation; other activated packages select dependency-closure-member, including nonworkspace path packages. A member used as a dependency remains snapshot-member. Actual producer/current activation/full source/lock/manifest/snapshot/custody joins are mandatory; membership is not inferred from null source, default-members, root/name/key/content/path equality or a caller witness. Package/member/used resolve/dependency ids join uniquely in that observation without parsing/deduplication/default/drop. All acquired candidates finish admission/rejection and all admitted candidates materialize whole before activation; inactive metadata omission is not a pruning license. Existing NKC-1/R3-MR1/CSJ-1 bytes and grant rules stay closed. Three actual synthetic fixture observations support this rule only; complete source/profile/namespace/failure/library/product/R3/effectiveL/O7/GT/qualification gates remain open.\n"
    }
  ],
